From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:07:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] mainmenu: the handheld's New World dialog as
 Minecraft's, with world types, difficulty and game rules

The handheld's dialog asked for the name, the seed, the game mode and a bonus chest, and always made
the game's default mapgen. It is laid out as Minecraft's Create New World now, in three tabs over
Create and Cancel:

- Game: the name, the game mode, the difficulty (Peaceful, Easy, Normal, Hard) and whether the mode
  can be changed in game.
- World: the world type (Default, Superflat, Large biomes, Amplified, Single biome, Valleys,
  Carpathian), a Customize page with caves, decorations, dungeons and the mapgen's own flags (and
  the biome, for Single biome), the seed, structures and the bonus chest.
- More: Minecraft's game rules: keep inventory, daylight cycle, mobs spawning, fire spreading, mobs
  changing blocks and natural regeneration.

The types are mapgen settings written to map_meta.txt when the world is made: Superflat is flat,
Valleys and Carpathian are those mapgens, the rest v7; Large biomes spreads the heat and humidity
noises 4 times; Amplified keeps the seas as Default and raises the hills and the mountains, more of
them and higher (from v7's noises over 4 km at one seed: mountains on 16% of the land instead of 11%,
the highest at 376 instead of 128); Single biome holds heat and humidity at one of Minetest Game's biomes (its shores, oceans
and underground share its point, so it is the nearest everywhere, and no biome is unregistered).

The choices go to world.mt for the game's mods (world_type, single_biome, generate_structures,
difficulty and one key per rule), and those that other mods read as settings also as
"setting.<name> = <value>": builtin/game/world_settings.lua sets them for the world's session before
the mods load, and restores the user's own at shutdown. Only bones_mode, enable_fire,
mob_difficulty, mobs_griefing, mobs_spawn, only_peaceful_mobs and time_speed, so that a world from
elsewhere can't change other settings. A setting is written only when the rule isn't the default.

Re-create fills in all of a world's choices, its Customize flags from map_meta.txt included. pt_BR
strings added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

